# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Linux AddressSanitizer build
# (CMakeLists.txt passes this file in LSAN_OPTIONS to every test).
#
# The X11 client libraries, which JUCE loads for windows and menus, keep
# per-display, locale, input-method and resource-database state until the
# process exits. The GUI test programs link them in sanitizer builds so they
# are never unloaded and their frames can be matched here. Suppressions name
# the X11/XCB entry points that create that state, not whole libraries, so a
# leak elsewhere that merely passes through libX11 is still reported.
leak:XOpenDisplay
leak:_XConnectXCB
leak:xcb_connect
leak:xcb_get_extension_data
leak:xcb_prefetch_extension_data
leak:XInitThreads
leak:XInitExtension
leak:XAddExtension
leak:XrmInitialize
leak:XrmGetStringDatabase
leak:XrmGetFileDatabase
leak:_XrmInternalStringToQuark
leak:XrmStringToQuark
leak:XGetDefault
leak:XSetLocaleModifiers
leak:XSupportsLocale
leak:_XlcCreateLC
leak:_XlcDefaultLoader
leak:_XlcCreateLocaleDataBase
leak:_XOpenLC
leak:XOpenIM
leak:_XimOpenIM
leak:_XimLocalOpenIM
leak:XCreateIC
leak:XkbGetMap
leak:XkbUseExtension
leak:XInternAtom
